WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:05.550
In Mexico City, a reader of Spanish
gets your Home page in English.

2
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:10.450
Its English is in the component, and
nothing in the project translates it.

3
00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:13.930
General Translation
covers the whole pipeline,

4
00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:17.050
from your code to
translation and delivery.

5
00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:23.390
Run npx gt init and wrap the content in
a T component, with no keys to write.

6
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.850
One command in your build writes the
German, Japanese and Spanish translations.

7
00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.090
Once your repository is connected,

8
00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:36.350
Locadex can open a pull request
with new translations when you push.

9
00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:40.230
In Mexico City, the Home
page now opens in Spanish.
